// This script builds all files in this archive in an appropriate order.
// Some non-essential parts may be skipped as commented below.
// The script is modular and calls corresponding build scripts in all subdirectories. Those script can be run on their own to build only the respective files.

// Because the files are build in dependency order, this file also doubles as documented table of contents for this archive.

// preparation: logging, settings, etc.
server on 8080
log html build.html
file build_config.msl

// ********************* fundamental concepts
// This includes formalizations of features like typing and equality.
// From these, various base languages are built. Usually each feature introduced below depends on one of these base languages.
file source/fundamentals/build.msl

// Propositional logics do not use any types or typed objects.
// Their base languages only introduces propositions.
file source/logic/propositional/build.msl
file source/logic/metalogic/build.msl

// FOL-like logics use (typed or untyped) terms.
file source/logic/fol_like/build.msl

// Type theory introduces various type/term constructing features of typed languages, in particular function types and lambda-abstraction.
file source/type_theory/buildNoEndo.msl

// HOL-like logics extend FOL-like logics with simple function types.
file source/logic/hol_like/build.msl

// Model theory describes base languages needed for model-theoretical semantics such as Kripke models in FOL.
file source/logic/model_theory/build.msl

// Category theory introduces the basic notions of categories.
// This is used in particular to obtain the theory of types and inherit abbreviations from it into typed languages.
build MMT/LATIN2 mmt-omdoc category_theory

// Multiple type theoretical features are based on endofunctors on the category of types, such as lists or sets over a type.
file source/type_theory/endofunctors/build.msl

// Set theory defines ZFC-style languages using FOL as the meta-theory.
file source/set_theory/build.msl

// Logic extensions formalizes various less common logical features.
file source/logic/other/build.msl

// Theory morphisms formalizing the Curry-Howard correspondence between logics and type theories.
build MMT/LATIN2 mmt-omdoc curry-howard

// Numbers
file source/domain_theories/numbers/build.msl

// The algebraic hierarchy based on FOL.
file source/domain_theories/algebra/build.msl

// Topology formalizes the various definitions of closure operators and topologies.
// These are interesting in their own and a case-study on theory morphisms, but also often used at the meta-level.
// They depend on PowerHOL.
build MMT/LATIN2 mmt-omdoc domain/theories/topology

// Meta-theorems stating the algebraic properties of logic, formalized as theory morphisms from algebraic to logical theories.
build MMT/LATIN2 mmt-omdoc algebraic_logic/pl_semilattice.mmt

// The set-theoretical semantics of logical and type-theoretical features, formalized as theory morphisms into set theory.
file source/set-theoretical_semantics/build.msl

